          "en": "because I'll then call a run on that prepared statement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.2,
          "end": 75.96000000000001,
          "en": "And now there we pass the concrete values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.96000000000001,
          "end": 78.75,
          "en": "for those question mark placeholders,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.75,
          "end": 81.633,
          "en": "so the email and the password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.19,
          "end": 86.58,
          "en": "And that will give us a result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.58,
          "end": 89.73,
          "en": "So we'll get a result of running this database query",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.73,
          "end": 92.34,
          "en": "and I then wanna return that result,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.34,
          "end": 95.94,
          "en": "or specifically there the last insert row ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.94,
          "end": 100.65299999999999,
          "en": "so the ID for that user that was now newly created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 102.21000000000001,
          "end": 104.00999999999999,
          "en": "Now this SQL statement here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.00999999999999,
          "end": 106.77000000000001,
          "en": "should be pretty self-explanatory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.77000000000001,
          "end": 111.27000000000001,
          "en": "And this DB thing, which I'm using here is in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 111.27000000000001,
          "end": 113.00999999999999,
          "en": "an object that's provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.00999999999999,
          "end": 115.8,
          "en": "by that better SQLite 3 package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.8,
          "end": 118.2,
          "en": "which gives us methods like the prepare",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.2,
          "end": 121.44,
          "en": "and run method here that allow us to interact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.44,
          "end": 123.603,
          "en": "with our SQLite database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.62,
          "end": 127.613,
          "en": "So that would create a new user and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.613,
          "end": 131.58,
          "en": "therefore in our auth actions JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.58,
          "end": 136.57999999999998,
          "en": "after validating the input, we could run create user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 136.92000000000002,
          "end": 139.59,
          "en": "So import this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.59,
          "end": 144.063,
          "en": "from that user JS file I just created in the lib folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.93,
          "end": 148.44,
          "en": "and then pass our validated email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.44,
          "end": 152.13,
          "en": "and password to this function to create that user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 152.13,
          "end": 154.26,
          "en": "That's how we could do it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 154.26,
          "end": 159.26,
          "en": "but this approach would have a very big flaw",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 159.63,
          "end": 162.6,
          "en": "and security problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 162.6,
          "end": 165.72,
          "en": "And do you have an idea what the problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 165.72,
          "end": 168.183,
          "en": "with this approach here would be?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 170.16,
          "end": 174.15,
          "en": "Well, the problem with creating a user like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 174.15,
          "end": 179.07,
          "en": "would be that we would take the password that was entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 179.07,
          "end": 180.99,
          "en": "by the user in the form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 180.99,
          "end": 183.84,
          "en": "and we would store it just like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 183.84,
          "end": 187.833,
          "en": "as plain text in the end, in the database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 189,
          "end": 193.11,
          "en": "which means that any employee, if they have access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 193.11,
          "end": 197.88,
          "en": "to that database, could extract the passwords of our users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 197.88,
          "end": 201.84,
          "en": "We, as the owner, could see the passwords of our users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 201.84,
          "end": 205.8,
          "en": "and our users probably wouldn't like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 205.8,
          "end": 210.36,
          "en": "And if our database ever gets compromised, gets attacked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 210.36,
          "end": 213.78,
          "en": "and hacked, then those attackers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 213.78,
          "end": 218.76,
          "en": "would retrieve emails and passwords stored in plain text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 218.76,
          "end": 222.93,
          "en": "and they could then try those email password combinations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 222.93,
          "end": 227.93,
          "en": "on other sites because people tend to reuse passwords.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 228.57,
          "end": 231.93,
          "en": "And therefore, as a very simple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 231.93,
          "end": 233.97,
          "en": "yet important rule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 233.97,
          "end": 238.97,
          "en": "you should never store plain text passwords.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 240.21,
          "end": 244.77,
          "en": "So we should not pass the password as it was entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 244.77,
          "end": 247.8,
          "en": "by the user into our database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 247.8,
          "end": 251.91,
          "en": "Instead, we should first hash it, so we should convert it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 251.91,
          "end": 254.61,
          "en": "to some strange looking string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 254.61,
          "end": 256.92,
          "en": "which can't be converted back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 256.92,
          "end": 261.9,
          "en": "so that if that string ever gets compromised,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 261.9,
          "end": 265.95,
          "en": "nobody knows what the original password was.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 265.95,
          "end": 268.83299999999997,
          "en": "And that's what we'll work on next.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
